>> title: Boston Baked Beans, Instant Pot
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, molasses, salt pork, new england, instant pot, pressure cooker, no soak
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot baked beans, pressure cooker baked beans, no soak baked beans, instant pot boston baked beans, Boston beans, molasses baked beans
>> servings: 8
>> dish: boston-baked-beans
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> time: 1 hr 55 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a bean held chalky by acid stays chalky however long the machine runs, and under the lid you cannot taste one to find out
>> step.1: A bean pot is doing flavour work this cannot copy. Here is what you get instead, and what you give up.
>> step.2: cook the navy beans from dry — 30 min at high pressure
>> step.3: wait out the natural release 20 min
>> step.4: stir the molasses in now, not before — 10 min at high pressure
>> step.5: wait out the natural release 10 min
>> step.6: reduce lid off 15 min until it holds

Five hours in a bean pot is not five hours of waiting.

Put @dried navy beans{1%lb}(450 g; dry, not soaked) into the #Instant Pot{} with @water{5%cups}(1.2 L), @salt pork{6%oz}(170 g; rind scored) and @yellow onion{1%medium}(chopped), lock the lid and ~pressure cook{30%min} at high pressure.

Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{20%min} until the pin drops.

Stir @molasses{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @dark brown sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @dry mustard{1%tsp}, @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)beans{}, lock the lid again and ~pressure cook{10%min}.

Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{10%min}, then open it.

Reduce @&(~1)beans{} on Sauté with the lid off ~reduce{15%min}, stirring now and then, until the liquid is a syrup that holds the trail of a spoon for a second.
